hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1475","Utbah bin Abdullah told us: I read to Malik, meaning Ibn Anas, on the authority of Sumayy, the client of Abu Bakr, who is Ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Samman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If only they knew what is in the darkness And in the morning I will come to them even if they crawl.”"
